# LucidPM reads these at startup (LucidPM/state.py). Copy to `.env` and edit for
# local development; leave `.env` absent to use the built-in local defaults
# shown below. `.env` is gitignored. A host that injects real environment
# variables (e.g. a container) overrides anything here.
#
# Syntax: KEY=value, one per line. Comments must be on their OWN line starting
# with `#` — a trailing/inline comment is treated as part of the value (a SQL
# password may legitimately contain `#`), so `LUCIDPM_SQL_LOGIN_TIMEOUT=30  # x`
# fails validation at startup. Wrap a value in matching single or double quotes
# to keep surrounding whitespace; one such pair is stripped, contents kept exact.

# --- Database connection ----------------------------------------------------
# SQL Server instance / host. Local default:
#LUCIDPM_SQL_SERVER=localhost\SQLEXPRESS
# Azure example:
#LUCIDPM_SQL_SERVER=lucidpm-sql-24899.database.windows.net

# Auth mode: "windows" (integrated, local only) or "sql" (username/password).
# For "sql": Cycle 2.2 smoke test may use the lucidadmin server login. The
# cloud build (Stage 3+) MUST use a dedicated contained, non-admin user
# (provisioned in BOTH databases if the Test/Prod toggle is kept) — see the
# PM cloud-migration knowledge share.
#LUCIDPM_SQL_AUTH=windows
#LUCIDPM_SQL_USER=lucidadmin
#LUCIDPM_SQL_PASSWORD=

# Deployment marker: unset / "local" for local dev, "cloud" inside Azure
# Container Apps. Not read by anything yet — reserved for Stage 5.3 Entra auth.
#LUCIDPM_ENV=local

# --- Secrets / config encryption -----------------------------------------
# Fernet key(s) for the stored SMTP password + Anthropic API key. Required
# before email or AI features work; the app still BOOTS without it.
# Comma-separated: the first key encrypts, all keys decrypt (MultiFernet).
#  - Fresh install: generate one —
#      python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
#  - Rotation / migration off the old DB key: LUCIDPM_FERNET_KEY=<new>,<old...>
#    then re-save each secret in Admin Settings on both DBs, then drop <old...>.
# In the cloud this is a Container Apps secret, never a committed value.
#LUCIDPM_FERNET_KEY=

# ODBC encryption. Local default yes/yes works for SQL Express with a self-
# signed cert. For Azure use yes / no (real managed certificate).
#LUCIDPM_SQL_ENCRYPT=yes
#LUCIDPM_SQL_TRUST_CERT=yes

# Login timeout in seconds (raise for a serverless Azure DB resuming from pause)
#LUCIDPM_SQL_LOGIN_TIMEOUT=30

# Connect-retry for Azure serverless auto-pause. Measured at Cycle 2.2
# (2026-09-10) against the real lucidpm-sql-24899 server: cold resumes took
# ~20-30s and ~78s, both recovered cleanly with the defaults below. This is
# extra attempts after the first; 0 restores single-attempt behaviour (max 10).
#LUCIDPM_SQL_CONNECT_RETRIES=8
# Base seconds between attempts (attempt k waits backoff * k: 4s, 8s, 12s...
# 32s across 8 retries, ~144s total budget; max 30).
#LUCIDPM_SQL_RETRY_BACKOFF=4

# --- Database selection ----------------------------------------------------
# The two databases the Test/Prod toggle switches between.
#LUCIDPM_PROD_DB=TenantCRM
#LUCIDPM_TEST_DB=TenantCRM_Test

# Optional: lock the app to ONE database and hide the Test/Prod toggle. Leave
# unset for local and for cloud dev (you still want the toggle). Set it only
# for a locked-down deployment.
#LUCIDPM_SINGLE_DB=TenantCRM

# --- Lease-document storage -------------------------------------------------
# "local" (default) keeps today's LeaseDocumentStorageRoot\Generated behavior.
# "azure_blob" stores generated packages plus newly uploaded source PDFs and
# split PDF sections in Azure Blob Storage. Existing source/section rows stay
# local until the one-time data migration is run.
# The connection string is for local Cycle 4.1 validation only; never commit it
# or put the full account key in a Container App. Cycle 4.2 must use a scoped
# SAS token or managed identity.
#LUCIDPM_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
#LUCIDPM_BLOB_CONNECTION_STRING=
#LUCIDPM_BLOB_CONTAINER=lucidpm-documents

# --- Example: local app against the Azure SQL databases (Cycle 2.2) -------
# Keeps the Test/Prod toggle. Use the contained, least-privilege app login
# (lucidpm_app — db_datareader + db_datawriter, created via
# db/azure_app_user.sql in BOTH databases), not the server admin (lucidadmin
# is for admin tasks / one-off smoke tests only).
# NOTE: a `.env` file here is read by EVERY `reflex run` from this checkout,
# on any port. For an ad-hoc Azure test that must not disturb your normal
# local app, set these as process env vars in one shell instead of creating a
# persistent `.env`. Start-LucidPM-Azure.ps1 (repo root, untracked) does this
# for you — prompts for the password, launches on 3002/8002. Equivalent by hand
# in PowerShell:
#   $env:LUCIDPM_SQL_SERVER = 'lucidpm-sql-24899.database.windows.net'
#   $env:LUCIDPM_SQL_AUTH = 'sql'; $env:LUCIDPM_SQL_USER = 'lucidpm_app'
#   $env:LUCIDPM_SQL_TRUST_CERT = 'no'
#   # LOGIN_TIMEOUT / CONNECT_RETRIES / RETRY_BACKOFF: the defaults above were
#   # measured against this exact server — no override needed.
#   # prompt for the password — do not paste it as a quoted literal (PowerShell
#   # expands $ and backticks inside "..."), and keep it out of shell history:
#   $sec = Read-Host 'SQL password' -AsSecureString
#   $env:LUCIDPM_SQL_PASSWORD = [System.Net.NetworkCredential]::new('', $sec).Password
#   & .\.venv\Scripts\reflex.exe run --frontend-port 3002 --backend-port 8002
# The vars die with that shell; a normal Start-LucidPM.ps1 from any other
# window still uses local SQL.
#LUCIDPM_SQL_SERVER=lucidpm-sql-24899.database.windows.net
#LUCIDPM_SQL_AUTH=sql
#LUCIDPM_SQL_USER=lucidpm_app
#LUCIDPM_SQL_PASSWORD=<the lucidpm_app password>
#LUCIDPM_SQL_TRUST_CERT=no
#LUCIDPM_PROD_DB=TenantCRM
#LUCIDPM_TEST_DB=TenantCRM_Test
